under the existing file lock. The historical 2026-04-29 curation audit directories were
backfilled into the ledger, and regression detection now treats quote-audit failures on
rejected rows as evidence for rejection rather than current accepted-record failures.
Verification: 91 quality-gate tests, 13 override-contract tests, reproducibility audit
across 243 records, and baseline-vs-current regression check all pass.
Impact: M | Effort: M

**RR-13 — Independent statistical adequacy assessment for the ingested registry** — DONE (2026-04-29)
The current registry is traceable and internally gated, but that does not prove it is a
complete/honest translation of the source corpus. Build an independent statistical
assessment lane: stratified sample over document, authority class, modality, lifecycle
bucket, and high-risk source shapes; blind human review against source windows; explicit
error taxonomy for omission, over-promotion, under-promotion, wrong modality/authority,
bad quote support, bad split/bundle shape, and duplicate/redundant records; acceptance
thresholds with confidence intervals. This should assess both accepted records and source
windows with no accepted output so omissions are measurable.
Completed as a same-agent first-pass review (not a strict external audit) in
`quality/adequacy/adequacy_2026-04-29-rr13-80-20/`. Result: 35/48 sampled records were
clean; 6/48 had major bad quote support, 6/48 were source-supported under-promotions due
quote-shape defects, and 1/48 had overstated authority/modality metadata. Section review
found 3/12 material-omission windows with 19 estimated missing actionable requirements.
Conclusion before repair: the registry was traceable, but not yet fit as a complete
actionable translation. The sampled blockers were then fixed directly in RR-14 to RR-16.
Impact: H | Effort: M

**RR-14 — Accepted records can have verbatim but insufficient quote support** — DONE (2026-04-29)
G1 proves each `exactSourceQuotes[]` string appears in the source, but it does not prove
the quote set supports the claim. RR-13 sampled accepted records where the claim inherits
normative force or referents from a parent/list heading not present in `exactSourceQuotes`
(examples: ICAO 4444 departing-aircraft and wake-table fragments, SafetySense22 item-level
readbacks, SERA.8015(e) item-level readbacks, Slovenia WILCO reference). Add a support-
sufficiency gate/review path and repair accepted records by including parent context or
demoting claims that cannot be supported by their cited quotes.
Direct repair added parent/list/table context to the affected accepted records and
recomputed their canonical IDs. Accepted quote-audit failures are now 0.
Impact: H | Effort: M

**RR-15 — Source-supported facts are under-promoted after quote-shape defects** — DONE (2026-04-29)
RR-13 found source-supported records left in `rejected/` because exact quotes had
typographic, line-break, ellipsis, or punctuation drift and curation could not edit identity
fields. This is honest for the malformed record but incomplete for downstream consumers
when no corrected accepted replacement exists. Examples include ICAO 4444 departure-
sequence factors, ICAO 4444 wake turbulence separation, SERA clearance-content item, and
Slovenia ROGER/WILCO/readback-order guidance. Add a corrected-replacement path that keeps
the malformed record rejected but emits a new canonical record with verbatim source quotes.
Direct repair promoted corrected canonical replacements for the sampled source-supported
records and added missing EGAST/Slovenia records from the reviewed source windows.
